{%- comment -%}
  The hub intro row: eyebrow, H2, body copy, and optionally the "Why Choose
  Us" rotator beside it.

  Lived inside hub-hero, which rendered the hero banner and this row as one
  section. That was fine until the brands page wanted its A–Z list between
  the two — a section cannot be split by template order, so the row had to
  become something both hub-hero and a standalone section could render. The
  markup is unchanged, so the five hubs that render it through hub-hero look
  exactly as they did.

  Accepts: eyebrow, heading, text, show_rotator, uid.

  uid is passed through rather than read from section.id because the snippet
  has no section of its own when rendered from a snippet context, and the
  rotator keys its state on that id.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if heading != blank or text != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The class follows the content: with the rotator beside it the row is the
    normal two-column grid, and without it .no-aside collapses to one, because
    a 1.25fr column of copy with dead space beside it is what the rotator's
    removal from the other hubs was avoiding in the first place.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="section-sm coll-intro"><div class="container coll-intro-grid{% unless show_rotator %} no-aside{% endunless %}">
    <div class="coll-intro-copy">
      {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="label">{{ eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if heading != blank -%}<h2 class="sec-title">{{ heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if text != blank -%}<div class="sec-sub coll-intro-body">{{ text }}</div>{%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if show_rotator -%}
      {% render 'why-choose-rotator', uid: uid %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div></section>
{%- endif -%}
